<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bolko I the Strict</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1253–<a href="/years/1301">1301</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Bolko I of Świdnica, Bolko I of Jawor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bolko I the Strict was a Silesian Piast duke, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-ii-the-bald">Bolesław II the Bald</a>. He received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawor">Jawor</a> in 1274, added <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swidnica">Świdnica</a> around 1291 and built a strong duchy along the Bohemian border, guarded by castles such as Bolków and Grodziec. He also founded the Cistercian abbey of Krzeszów. His duchy remained independent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> longer than any other in Silesia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bolko-i-the-strict.jpg" alt="Bolko I the Strict" width="320" height="295" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bolko_I_Surowy_seal_1298.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
